{"id":"sh/fapwfyds","kind":"textbox","name":"Google Shape;534;p58","position":{"left":41.33,"top":353.33,"width":374.67,"height":276},"text":"A reproducible baseline\nAudit one EEG subset. Fit a spectral logistic classifier with participant-grouped splits. Include majority and sleep-stage controls.","style":{"fontSize":24,"typeface":"Inter SemiBold","color":"#FFFFFF","bold":true,"alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect"},
{"id":"sh/1cj2d8b6","kind":"textbox","name":"Content Placeholder 1","position":{"left":864,"top":353.33,"width":374.67,"height":276},"text":"An explanatory demo\nShow signals, scores and failures. Include a short report and a walkthrough the student can give without relying on AI-written explanations.","style":{"fontSize":24,"typeface":"Inter SemiBold","color":"#FFFFFF","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}},
{"id":"sh/0ba143al","kind":"textbox","name":"Content Placeholder 2","position":{"left":452.67,"top":353.33,"width":374.67,"height":276},"text":"One transformer study\nAfter the baseline works, compare mean pooling with learned time-bin weighting. Keep the same features and split. A clear negative result counts.\n","style":{"fontSize":24,"typeface":"Inter SemiBold","color":"#FFFFFF","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}},
